"{\n  \"reasoning\": \"To meet GBW: gm1 >= 2\u03c0\u00b715MHz\u00b72pF \u2248 188\u00b5S. With gm/Id = 10, each input transistor needs Id = gm1/10 \u2248 19\u00b5A, so Itail \u2248 38\u00b5A (choose 40\u00b5A for margin). Power = 3.3V\u00b72\u00b740\u00b5A \u2248 264\u00b5W < 500\u00b5W. Gain depends on output resistances: choose long channel NMOS (L=2\u00b5m, gm/gds\u2248580) and long channel PMOS (L=2\u00b5m, gm/gds\u22481258). Parallel resistance \u2248 397 \u2192 A0 \u2248 397 (>251 required for 48dB). Slew rate = Itail/CL = 40\u00b5A/2pF = 20V/\u00b5s, ample. Output swing >1.5V is feasible with Vdsat \u22480.2\u20110.3V for both devices. Phase margin satisfied as mirror pole is pushed low by high L PMOS. Thus the chosen operating points meet all specs.\",\n  \"gmid1\": 10,\n  \"L1_um\": 2.0,\n  \"gmid3\": 10,\n  \"L3_um\": 2.0,\n  \"gmid5\": 10,\n  \"L5_um\": 0.5,\n  \"Itail_uA\": 40\n}"